initial N-row build cancel):

  scan path, 1,000 rows   (7,692,622,869 - 523,525,905) / 20 = 358,454,848
  delta path, 1,000 rows    (169,984,056 - 169,537,118) / 20 =      22,347
  ratio                                                       ≈ 16,040x

  scan path,   500 rows  (1,216,117,393 -   265,273,889) / 10 =  95,084,350
  scan path, 2,000 rows (15,235,304,665 - 1,536,365,826) / 10 = 1,369,893,884

  500 -> 1,000  3.77x     1,000 -> 2,000  3.82x     => QUADRATIC in N.

Cross-check on the 1,000-row scan figure without the slope: the delta run's
baseline is (169,537,118 - 22,347) = 169,514,771 Ir of node startup plus the
1,000-row build, so one scan pass on top of the same baseline is
523,525,905 - 169,514,771 = 354,011,134 Ir — within 1.2% of the slope, and the
residual is the list growing 1,000 -> 1,021 across the 21 rounds.
